\title{The algebraic branch: interpolation to rank sums}
\taxon{Overview}
\meta{dependencies}{None.}
\meta{provenance}{Expository organization and source review, 9 October 2026.}

\p{This argument does not involve drawings. The only geometric-looking objects are subspaces of a finite-dimensional real vector space. The route is evaluation dimensions, rank loss at constraint nodes, multiplicity of polynomial determinants, and a degree count. Graphs of linear maps then turn intersection dimensions into matrix ranks.}

